# UST.G3BJ Transcendental-Arc Discriminant-Avoidance and Integral-Transport Theorem

## Result

The G3BI start member is now joined to fixed B67/B89 `F0` by one explicit
smooth path that works for every Archimedean embedding of `Q(gamma)`:

```text
F_a = F0 + a C,
C   = F_G3BI - F0,
a(t)=1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t),  0 <= t <= 1.
```

At `t=0` this is the root-containing G3BI member; at `t=1` it is fixed `F0`.
Every intermediate member is smooth. The path therefore defines an integral
Gauss-Manin isomorphism and an exact abstract terminal class
`PT_G3BJ(z4)`. It does not emit that class in B89 coordinates or compute its
248-row readout.

## 1. Why the Discriminant Is Algebraic and Finite

The singular eta9 sections form a Zariski-closed discriminant over the
algebraic closure of `Q`: take the critical incidence on the projective
`K3 x E` carrier and project it properly to coefficient space. Restrict this
discriminant to the algebraic correction line `F0+aC`.

The line is not contained in the discriminant because both `a=0` and `a=1`
are certified smooth. Its projective intersection with the discriminant is
therefore a finite algebraic scheme. In any complex embedding, every finite
critical parameter `a` is an algebraic complex number.

## 2. The Transcendental Arc

For `0<t<1`, consider

```text
a(t)=1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t).
```

Suppose `a(t)` were algebraic. Its real part `1-t` would be algebraic, so `t`
would be algebraic. Then `t(1-t)` is a nonzero algebraic number. Since `pi` is
transcendental, `pi*t*(1-t)` is transcendental, contradicting algebraicity of
the imaginary part. If `t` is transcendental, the real part is already
transcendental. Thus every interior `a(t)` is transcendental.

All critical parameters are algebraic, so none lies on the arc. The endpoints
are smooth by G3BI. This proves complete discriminant avoidance without
computing or isolating the 5,976 generic critical values.

The positive imaginary sign fixes the upper arc and hence a reproducible
marking convention. It is not a physical parameter: another path changes a
lift only by integral monodromy/period data, while the Deligne quotient is
path-independent at the declared tier.

## 3. Integral Transport

Restrict the smooth proper eta9 family to the G3BJ arc. Ehresmann local
triviality makes the rank-1,509 integral Gauss-Manin local system constant
along this interval up to its path-oriented canonical transport. In
particular, the G3BG source

```text
z4=(-e2+2f2) tensor u_B
```

has a well-defined integral terminal image

```text
PT_G3BJ(z4)
```

in the fixed B89 fiber. This closes path selection and the existence of the
integral one-vector map. It does not execute the map in the frozen B89 basis.

## Frontier Consequence

The live computation no longer needs:

- another root-containing start search;
- a 5,976-value discriminant enumeration merely to choose a path;
- a physical Archimedean embedding selector for path existence; or
- transport of a full rank-1,509 frame.

It now needs only:

1. rigorous continuation of the one vector `z4` along the exact G3BJ arc;
2. terminal integral B89 coordinates or a certified meridian word;
3. the normalized 248-row readout; and
4. the G3BD quotient decision.

## Claim Boundary

G3BJ does not emit:

- the rank-1,509 coordinates of `PT_G3BJ(z4)`;
- a B89 meridian word;
- a numerical or interval Gauss-Manin continuation;
- the normalized 248-coordinate readout;
- a physical selection among the six embeddings;
- a decision of `beta_C`; or
- closure of `B.ETA9.01` or `B.ETA9.02`.

